{
  "summary": "Refactors wallet loading, creation, restoration, verification, and migration across the wallet subsystem to uniformly return util::Result and util::ResultPtr. It eliminates mutable out-parameters for database status enums, bilingual error strings, and warning vectors. As part of this standardization, DatabaseStatus is renamed to DatabaseError with its unused success state removed.",
  "problem": "Wallet initialization and loading functions across the stack handle errors inconsistently, passing multiple mutable out-parameters for status codes, error strings, and lists of warnings. This creates cumbersome function signatures and boilerplate error-propagation code across wallet internals, RPC handlers, and GUI controllers.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author description: 'Wallet loading functions up and down the stack have lots of error and warning parameters, and return error information in different ways. This PR makes them uniformly return util::Result, without changing behavior.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#25665",
      "#26022"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "This PR is stacked on #25665 and #26022, including commits that enhance util::Result to support error payload types, warning messages, and pointer dereferencing sugar. It also includes a scripted-diff commit replacing DatabaseStatus with DatabaseError.",
  "changed_since_previous": "Rebased onto master to incorporate recent wallet architectural changes (such as the splitting of CWallet::Create), and updated base commits with a CI configuration workaround for GCC maybe-uninitialized compiler warnings.",
  "card": "This pull request refactors wallet loading, creation, restoration, and migration functions across the wallet subsystem to uniformly return util::Result and util::ResultPtr. It removes disparate out-parameters for database status codes, bilingual error strings, and warning vectors, standardizing error reporting without changing behavior. The PR is an internal refactoring with no reported bug fixes or user-visible functional changes. It depends on base PRs #25665 and #26022 for extensions to the util::Result template.",
